1
00:00:00,090 --> 00:00:01,650
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:01,650 --> 00:00:03,760
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:03,760 --> 00:00:04,990
don't accept that.

4
00:00:05,140 --> 00:00:06,510
I've been a
home health aide

5
00:00:06,510 --> 00:00:08,040
for twenty-two years.

6
00:00:08,100 --> 00:00:10,240
Going house to house all
day,

7
00:00:10,240 --> 00:00:11,550
kneeling to help my
clients

8
00:00:11,550 --> 00:00:13,220
with their shoes and their
baths,

9
00:00:13,220 --> 00:00:14,850
helping them up out of
chairs more

10
00:00:14,850 --> 00:00:16,720
times than I could ever
count.

11
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:18,240
That's a lot of years

12
00:00:18,240 --> 00:00:19,430
on a pair of knees.

13
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:20,790
I had my right knee

14
00:00:20,790 --> 00:00:22,460
replaced two years ago.

15
00:00:22,560 --> 00:00:24,300
It has hurt every day
since.

16
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:25,660
Not surgery pain.

17
00:00:25,910 --> 00:00:27,410
I know what that felt
like,

18
00:00:27,410 --> 00:00:28,520
and it went away.

19
00:00:28,620 --> 00:00:29,740
This is different.

20
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:30,720
Tight.

21
00:00:30,880 --> 00:00:31,690
Full.

22
00:00:31,760 --> 00:00:32,600
Like a band around

23
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:34,310
the joint that never
loosens.

24
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:35,550
And for two years

25
00:00:35,550 --> 00:00:37,160
I've been told the same
thing.

26
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:38,260
Give it time.

27
00:00:39,170 --> 00:00:40,970
At six weeks it was
swelling,

28
00:00:40,970 --> 00:00:42,280
and swelling is normal.

29
00:00:42,320 --> 00:00:43,140
At three months,

30
00:00:43,140 --> 00:00:44,250
give it six.

31
00:00:44,380 --> 00:00:45,640
At six months,

32
00:00:45,640 --> 00:00:47,670
some knees take a full
year.

33
00:00:48,240 --> 00:00:49,180
At a year,

34
00:00:49,180 --> 00:00:51,190
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

35
00:00:51,570 --> 00:00:52,890
And I didn't just wait.

36
00:00:52,930 --> 00:00:54,480
We went down the list.

37
00:00:54,520 --> 00:00:56,100
More physical therapy.

38
00:00:56,600 --> 00:00:57,620
Every session,

39
00:00:57,620 --> 00:00:59,380
every exercise at home.

40
00:00:59,560 --> 00:01:00,730
I got stronger.

41
00:01:00,910 --> 00:01:02,610
The tightness never moved.

42
00:01:02,650 --> 00:01:04,080
The pain pills helped,

43
00:01:04,080 --> 00:01:05,320
and that was the problem.

44
00:01:06,050 --> 00:01:08,180
I'm already on enough
every morning,

45
00:01:08,180 --> 00:01:09,130
and nobody could tell me

46
00:01:09,130 --> 00:01:10,330
when I'd get to stop.

47
00:01:10,370 --> 00:01:11,610
Then a nerve block.

48
00:01:11,870 --> 00:01:13,570
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

49
00:01:13,690 --> 00:01:15,230
And after that, a second

50
00:01:15,230 --> 00:01:16,320
operation to go back

51
00:01:16,320 --> 00:01:17,940
in and do it over.

52
00:01:18,100 --> 00:01:19,060
I said no.

53
00:01:19,230 --> 00:01:20,970
Every morning I pulled on
my scrubs

54
00:01:20,970 --> 00:01:21,920
and my knee felt like

55
00:01:21,920 --> 00:01:23,870
a band was wrapped around
it,

56
00:01:23,870 --> 00:01:26,240
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

57
00:01:26,620 --> 00:01:27,920
Every morning I took
something

58
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:28,850
for it and drove

59
00:01:28,850 --> 00:01:30,610
to my first client's
house.

60
00:01:30,660 --> 00:01:32,100
Couldn't do the stairs,

61
00:01:32,100 --> 00:01:33,260
couldn't stand at the
counter

62
00:01:33,260 --> 00:01:34,750
long enough to finish
dinner,

63
00:01:34,750 --> 00:01:36,200
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's

64
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:38,400
game without shifting
every two minutes.

65
00:01:38,530 --> 00:01:40,480
It woke me at night,

66
00:01:40,480 --> 00:01:42,460
and it turned ordinary
things,

67
00:01:42,460 --> 00:01:43,560
like getting in the car

68
00:01:43,560 --> 00:01:44,990
or up off the couch,

69
00:01:44,990 --> 00:01:46,080
into a decision.

70
00:01:46,370 --> 00:01:47,580
After a long and serious

71
00:01:47,580 --> 00:01:48,840
talk with my husband,

72
00:01:48,840 --> 00:01:50,550
I went back in one more
time.

73
00:01:50,590 --> 00:01:51,710
That was the fourth set

74
00:01:51,710 --> 00:01:53,190
of X-rays on this knee.

75
00:01:53,390 --> 00:01:55,760
And like the three before
it,

76
00:01:55,760 --> 00:01:58,370
the answer was everything
looks great.

77
00:01:58,540 --> 00:02:00,840
No loosening, no
infection,

78
00:02:00,840 --> 00:02:01,900
nothing wrong.

79
00:02:02,140 --> 00:02:03,340
Only this time there

80
00:02:03,340 --> 00:02:04,710
was no new number.

81
00:02:04,930 --> 00:02:05,720
Nobody said

82
00:02:05,720 --> 00:02:07,290
give it another six
months.

83
00:02:07,330 --> 00:02:09,120
There was nothing left to
give it.

84
00:02:09,170 --> 00:02:10,230
I sat in the parking

85
00:02:10,230 --> 00:02:11,290
lot for a while.

86
00:02:11,410 --> 00:02:12,890
Okay, I thought.

87
00:02:12,970 --> 00:02:14,250
Then explain this.

88
00:02:14,580 --> 00:02:16,480
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

89
00:02:16,480 --> 00:02:17,980
I hit my breaking point.

90
00:02:18,020 --> 00:02:20,080
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

91
00:02:20,410 --> 00:02:21,770
I'd been to five clients'

92
00:02:21,770 --> 00:02:22,950
houses that day.

93
00:02:23,080 --> 00:02:24,850
Everyone in the house was
asleep

94
00:02:24,850 --> 00:02:26,550
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

95
00:02:26,550 --> 00:02:27,790
with my leg up,

96
00:02:27,790 --> 00:02:29,250
trying to find any angle
where

97
00:02:29,250 --> 00:02:30,350
it didn't feel like
something

98
00:02:30,350 --> 00:02:31,540
was wrapped around my knee

99
00:02:31,540 --> 00:02:32,440
and tightening.

100
00:02:32,780 --> 00:02:35,200
My husband didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

101
00:02:35,320 --> 00:02:36,960
By then I'd stopped
telling him.

102
00:02:37,560 --> 00:02:38,600
And I just thought,

103
00:02:38,600 --> 00:02:40,250
is this really my life
now?

104
00:02:40,290 --> 00:02:41,750
I can't live like this.

105
00:02:41,900 --> 00:02:43,590
So I made myself a
promise.

106
00:02:43,630 --> 00:02:44,440
I wouldn't go a day

107
00:02:44,440 --> 00:02:45,970
without looking for an
answer.

108
00:02:46,140 --> 00:02:48,360
And when I found one,

109
00:02:48,360 --> 00:02:49,430
I'd share it with everyone

110
00:02:49,430 --> 00:02:50,810
going through the same
thing.

111
00:02:50,850 --> 00:02:52,190
So I got my laptop

112
00:02:52,190 --> 00:02:53,880
out and went looking.

113
00:02:53,930 --> 00:02:55,080
Not for a product.

114
00:02:55,260 --> 00:02:56,440
For an explanation.

115
00:02:56,620 --> 00:02:58,300
Mayo Clinic forums,

116
00:02:58,300 --> 00:03:00,740
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

117
00:03:00,740 --> 00:03:03,400
doctor videos, medical
animations.

118
00:03:03,720 --> 00:03:04,710
And that's when I found

119
00:03:04,710 --> 00:03:06,390
a video from a physical
therapist

120
00:03:06,390 --> 00:03:06,930
named Dr.

121
00:03:06,970 --> 00:03:09,130
Steven Salinger, whose own
wife

122
00:03:09,130 --> 00:03:10,780
had been through exactly
this.

123
00:03:10,970 --> 00:03:12,440
But before I say anything
else,

124
00:03:12,440 --> 00:03:14,090
I want to be straight with
you.

125
00:03:14,770 --> 00:03:16,710
You've already had
something work fast.

126
00:03:16,950 --> 00:03:17,590
The ice.

127
00:03:17,790 --> 00:03:19,220
The first week of a new
pill.

128
00:03:19,260 --> 00:03:20,820
The good day after a
session.

129
00:03:20,900 --> 00:03:21,920
Then it wore off.

130
00:03:21,960 --> 00:03:24,060
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

131
00:03:24,330 --> 00:03:26,030
Fast relief isn't relief.

132
00:03:26,070 --> 00:03:27,110
It's a preview.

133
00:03:27,410 --> 00:03:28,540
So I'm not going to tell

134
00:03:28,540 --> 00:03:29,990
you this works fast.

135
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:30,950
It doesn't.

136
00:03:31,520 --> 00:03:33,430
But if you're willing to
be patient,

137
00:03:33,430 --> 00:03:34,350
and to look at what's

138
00:03:34,350 --> 00:03:36,040
going on around your new
knee

139
00:03:36,040 --> 00:03:37,790
instead of inside it,
there

140
00:03:37,790 --> 00:03:40,340
is a real reason it still
hurts.

141
00:03:40,380 --> 00:03:42,530
And something you can do
about it.

142
00:03:42,810 --> 00:03:44,570
Let me explain what he
said,

143
00:03:44,570 --> 00:03:45,950
because this is what
changed

144
00:03:45,950 --> 00:03:47,340
everything for me.

145
00:03:47,610 --> 00:03:49,410
He started with the
basics.

146
00:03:49,580 --> 00:03:51,140
A knee replacement takes
out

147
00:03:51,140 --> 00:03:53,050
the worn joint surfaces
and puts

148
00:03:53,050 --> 00:03:54,540
in metal and plastic.

149
00:03:54,670 --> 00:03:56,440
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

150
00:03:56,440 --> 00:03:58,120
you had before the
operation.

151
00:03:58,200 --> 00:03:59,660
That part I already knew.

152
00:04:00,320 --> 00:04:01,740
But then he explained
something

153
00:04:01,740 --> 00:04:03,340
nobody had ever told me.

154
00:04:03,380 --> 00:04:04,540
He said,

155
00:04:04,540 --> 00:04:06,180
think about a swollen foot

156
00:04:06,180 --> 00:04:07,240
inside a shoe.

157
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:08,630
The shoe didn't shrink.

158
00:04:08,690 --> 00:04:11,550
Your foot is taking up
more room,

159
00:04:11,550 --> 00:04:13,210
so everything feels
cramped

160
00:04:13,210 --> 00:04:14,860
and tight and squeezed.

161
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:16,400
Your new knee sits

162
00:04:16,400 --> 00:04:17,870
in a limited space with
living

163
00:04:17,870 --> 00:04:19,740
tissue packed all around
it.

164
00:04:19,930 --> 00:04:21,800
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

165
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:23,480
had to work through that
tissue.

166
00:04:23,640 --> 00:04:25,880
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

167
00:04:26,540 --> 00:04:28,460
At first that's normal.

168
00:04:28,730 --> 00:04:30,470
But in some people that
swelling can

169
00:04:30,470 --> 00:04:33,090
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

170
00:04:33,130 --> 00:04:34,910
And swollen tissue takes
up more

171
00:04:34,910 --> 00:04:36,760
room than calm tissue
does.

172
00:04:36,890 --> 00:04:38,920
So when you bend,

173
00:04:38,920 --> 00:04:41,240
that tissue gets
compressed.

174
00:04:41,460 --> 00:04:42,840
When you straighten,

175
00:04:42,840 --> 00:04:44,320
it gets pulled tight.

176
00:04:44,400 --> 00:04:45,360
That's the band.

177
00:04:45,400 --> 00:04:47,510
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

178
00:04:47,620 --> 00:04:48,560
And you start being

179
00:04:48,560 --> 00:04:49,600
the one who says,

180
00:04:49,600 --> 00:04:50,730
you go ahead.

181
00:04:50,980 --> 00:04:52,080
I'll stay here.

182
00:04:52,350 --> 00:04:53,980
And that's exactly why so
much

183
00:04:53,980 --> 00:04:55,700
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

184
00:04:56,300 --> 00:04:58,260
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

185
00:04:58,260 --> 00:04:59,170
around the knee.

186
00:04:59,460 --> 00:05:00,350
Worth doing,

187
00:05:00,350 --> 00:05:01,290
and I'd done it.

188
00:05:01,680 --> 00:05:03,130
It does nothing about
tissue

189
00:05:03,130 --> 00:05:04,240
taking up room.

190
00:05:04,760 --> 00:05:06,140
A nerve block quiets

191
00:05:06,140 --> 00:05:08,470
the nerve carrying the
signal.

192
00:05:08,570 --> 00:05:10,720
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

193
00:05:10,870 --> 00:05:12,390
But when that irritated
tissue

194
00:05:12,390 --> 00:05:13,910
finally calms down,

195
00:05:13,910 --> 00:05:15,310
it holds less fluid,

196
00:05:15,310 --> 00:05:16,830
and it takes up less room.

197
00:05:17,150 --> 00:05:18,630
Less room taken up means

198
00:05:18,630 --> 00:05:20,490
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

199
00:05:21,260 --> 00:05:23,090
That's what takes the
pressure off.

200
00:05:23,250 --> 00:05:24,390
After two years of this,

201
00:05:24,390 --> 00:05:26,040
it finally made sense.

202
00:05:26,780 --> 00:05:28,620
The problem was never the
new knee.

203
00:05:28,660 --> 00:05:31,020
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

204
00:05:31,160 --> 00:05:32,880
He calls it the squeeze.

205
00:05:33,010 --> 00:05:35,560
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

206
00:05:35,700 --> 00:05:36,880
I'd bought knee sleeves,

207
00:05:36,880 --> 00:05:38,970
compression braces,
creams,

208
00:05:38,970 --> 00:05:40,400
half of Amazon really,

209
00:05:40,400 --> 00:05:41,860
and all any of it gave me

210
00:05:41,860 --> 00:05:42,690
was an hour.

211
00:05:42,930 --> 00:05:43,890
I even looked at going

212
00:05:43,890 --> 00:05:45,780
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

213
00:05:46,010 --> 00:05:47,620
But at $200 a session

214
00:05:47,620 --> 00:05:49,860
with nothing covered by
insurance,

215
00:05:49,860 --> 00:05:51,280
that was a quick no.

216
00:05:51,950 --> 00:05:53,320
Then one night I went

217
00:05:53,320 --> 00:05:54,720
back to that knee
replacement

218
00:05:54,720 --> 00:05:56,790
group and actually read
it.

219
00:05:56,860 --> 00:05:57,850
Thousands of people,

220
00:05:57,850 --> 00:05:59,110
years out from surgery,

221
00:05:59,110 --> 00:06:01,460
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

222
00:06:01,460 --> 00:06:02,960
nobody could explain.

223
00:06:03,720 --> 00:06:05,670
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

224
00:06:05,670 --> 00:06:07,610
the same thing kept coming
up.

225
00:06:07,720 --> 00:06:08,930
This one device,

226
00:06:08,930 --> 00:06:10,270
and people saying it was
the first

227
00:06:10,270 --> 00:06:11,570
thing that made a
difference.

228
00:06:11,980 --> 00:06:13,960
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

229
00:06:13,960 --> 00:06:15,900
alright, here it comes,

230
00:06:15,900 --> 00:06:17,340
she's selling me
something,

231
00:06:17,340 --> 00:06:18,970
let me shut that down
right now.

232
00:06:19,010 --> 00:06:20,650
I'm only here because I
made myself

233
00:06:20,650 --> 00:06:22,670
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

234
00:06:22,670 --> 00:06:23,590
that if I ever found

235
00:06:23,590 --> 00:06:24,780
something that helped,

236
00:06:24,780 --> 00:06:25,720
I'd say so.

237
00:06:26,670 --> 00:06:29,210
It's called the KenRelief
Red

238
00:06:29,210 --> 00:06:31,080
Light Therapy Wrap.

239
00:06:31,730 --> 00:06:33,790
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

240
00:06:33,900 --> 00:06:34,820
It looked like the cheap

241
00:06:34,820 --> 00:06:36,180
knee sleeves off Amazon

242
00:06:36,180 --> 00:06:37,700
that did nothing for me.

243
00:06:37,920 --> 00:06:39,530
But I went to their
website anyway,

244
00:06:39,530 --> 00:06:40,320
just to see what all

245
00:06:40,320 --> 00:06:41,520
the fuss was about.

246
00:06:41,650 --> 00:06:43,230
It's the same red light
therapy

247
00:06:43,230 --> 00:06:45,510
clinics charge $200 a
session

248
00:06:45,510 --> 00:06:47,720
for, off machines that
cost

249
00:06:47,720 --> 00:06:49,140
fifty thousand dollars,

250
00:06:49,140 --> 00:06:50,030
in a wrap you plug

251
00:06:50,030 --> 00:06:51,260
into the wall at home.

252
00:06:51,380 --> 00:06:52,940
Two hundred and forty
lights.

253
00:06:53,020 --> 00:06:55,150
Red at 660 nanometers

254
00:06:55,150 --> 00:06:57,550
and near-infrared at 850,

255
00:06:57,550 --> 00:06:59,590
run together for the
strongest effect.

256
00:07:00,280 --> 00:07:01,570
Four strength levels.

257
00:07:01,800 --> 00:07:03,630
A five to thirty minute
timer.

258
00:07:03,880 --> 00:07:05,510
Then I saw the guarantee.

259
00:07:05,620 --> 00:07:06,860
Ninety days.

260
00:07:06,940 --> 00:07:08,950
Results or your money
back,

261
00:07:08,950 --> 00:07:11,410
no questions, no store
credit,

262
00:07:11,410 --> 00:07:13,090
and you don't even send it
back.

263
00:07:13,220 --> 00:07:15,340
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

264
00:07:15,340 --> 00:07:16,960
days to change my mind.

265
00:07:17,830 --> 00:07:18,990
There wasn't much to lose,

266
00:07:18,990 --> 00:07:19,990
so I ordered it.

267
00:07:20,030 --> 00:07:21,300
Two of them, actually.

268
00:07:21,480 --> 00:07:23,240
Only the right knee was
replaced,

269
00:07:23,240 --> 00:07:25,120
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

270
00:07:25,120 --> 00:07:26,730
and I'd done it for two
years.

271
00:07:27,030 --> 00:07:28,950
The left one was carrying
the difference.

272
00:07:28,990 --> 00:07:29,560
When it came,

273
00:07:29,560 --> 00:07:31,560
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

274
00:07:31,560 --> 00:07:32,660
because I'd been let down
too

275
00:07:32,660 --> 00:07:34,280
many times to get excited.

276
00:07:34,330 --> 00:07:35,900
What I felt was warmth.

277
00:07:36,630 --> 00:07:38,450
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

278
00:07:38,490 --> 00:07:40,240
More like it was coming
from inside

279
00:07:40,240 --> 00:07:42,070
the knee and spreading
around it.

280
00:07:42,110 --> 00:07:43,200
And that was it.

281
00:07:43,380 --> 00:07:45,190
That was the whole
experience.

282
00:07:45,600 --> 00:07:46,760
When I took it off,

283
00:07:46,760 --> 00:07:47,660
I'll be honest,

284
00:07:47,660 --> 00:07:49,260
nothing dramatic had
happened.

285
00:07:49,390 --> 00:07:51,080
And after what that video
said,

286
00:07:51,080 --> 00:07:53,020
that's exactly what I
expected.

287
00:07:53,140 --> 00:07:54,160
What was different

288
00:07:54,160 --> 00:07:54,950
was that for the first

289
00:07:54,950 --> 00:07:56,240
time in two years

290
00:07:56,240 --> 00:07:57,820
I'd done something for my
knee

291
00:07:57,820 --> 00:07:58,990
instead of to it.

292
00:07:59,070 --> 00:08:00,040
Twenty minutes,

293
00:08:00,040 --> 00:08:01,140
in my own chair.

294
00:08:01,320 --> 00:08:03,290
No drive, no copay.

295
00:08:03,420 --> 00:08:04,840
They say twenty minutes.

296
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:06,120
I did thirty,

297
00:08:06,120 --> 00:08:07,330
twice a day,

298
00:08:07,330 --> 00:08:09,190
lowest setting that first
week.

299
00:08:09,360 --> 00:08:10,820
I put it on the calendar.

300
00:08:11,030 --> 00:08:12,130
The first week,

301
00:08:12,130 --> 00:08:12,950
I couldn't have told

302
00:08:12,950 --> 00:08:14,390
you if anything was
happening.

303
00:08:14,480 --> 00:08:15,370
I tried not to get

304
00:08:15,370 --> 00:08:16,360
my hopes up.

305
00:08:16,540 --> 00:08:18,050
I'd had things help for a
week

306
00:08:18,050 --> 00:08:19,070
and then stop.

307
00:08:19,110 --> 00:08:20,610
But somewhere in the
second week

308
00:08:20,610 --> 00:08:21,850
I noticed I'd come down

309
00:08:21,850 --> 00:08:23,890
the stairs without holding
the rail.

310
00:08:24,140 --> 00:08:25,650
I hadn't decided to.

311
00:08:25,740 --> 00:08:26,950
I just did it,

312
00:08:26,950 --> 00:08:28,380
then stopped halfway down

313
00:08:28,380 --> 00:08:29,690
because I realized.

314
00:08:29,930 --> 00:08:31,610
By the end of the fourth
week

315
00:08:31,610 --> 00:08:32,700
I'd slept through the
night

316
00:08:32,700 --> 00:08:34,000
four times running.

317
00:08:34,550 --> 00:08:35,510
I stood at the counter

318
00:08:35,510 --> 00:08:36,560
and finished making dinner

319
00:08:36,560 --> 00:08:38,060
without looking for the
stool.

320
00:08:38,270 --> 00:08:39,650
None of that is dramatic.

321
00:08:39,790 --> 00:08:40,510
All of it was gone

322
00:08:40,510 --> 00:08:41,660
for two years.

323
00:08:41,750 --> 00:08:43,210
A few weeks later my
husband asked

324
00:08:43,210 --> 00:08:44,020
if I wanted to walk

325
00:08:44,020 --> 00:08:45,430
the long way around the
block.

326
00:08:45,640 --> 00:08:46,390
And for the first time

327
00:08:46,390 --> 00:08:47,390
in two years,

328
00:08:47,390 --> 00:08:48,270
I said yes.

329
00:08:48,650 --> 00:08:50,130
I wanted to understand
why,

330
00:08:50,130 --> 00:08:51,490
so I read the whole thing.

331
00:08:51,650 --> 00:08:53,190
It comes down to four
steps.

332
00:08:53,230 --> 00:08:53,840
One.

333
00:08:53,930 --> 00:08:55,330
The tissue around a new
knee can

334
00:08:55,330 --> 00:08:57,690
stay inflamed long after
surgery is over.

335
00:08:58,510 --> 00:08:59,160
Two.

336
00:08:59,200 --> 00:09:01,420
Inflamed tissue holds
extra fluid,

337
00:09:01,420 --> 00:09:02,330
so it takes up more

338
00:09:02,330 --> 00:09:03,360
room than it should.

339
00:09:03,470 --> 00:09:04,180
Three.

340
00:09:04,340 --> 00:09:05,910
There's only so much room
in there.

341
00:09:05,990 --> 00:09:07,450
Bending compresses it.

342
00:09:07,550 --> 00:09:09,180
Straightening pulls it
tight.

343
00:09:09,530 --> 00:09:10,800
That's the squeeze.

344
00:09:11,090 --> 00:09:11,660
Four.

345
00:09:11,700 --> 00:09:13,240
Red and near-infrared
light have been

346
00:09:13,240 --> 00:09:15,210
studied for calming that
inflammation,

347
00:09:15,210 --> 00:09:16,340
so the swelling and the
pressure

348
00:09:16,340 --> 00:09:17,530
can come down with it.

349
00:09:17,700 --> 00:09:19,230
In a randomized trial,

350
00:09:19,230 --> 00:09:20,960
patients given light
therapy after

351
00:09:20,960 --> 00:09:21,850
a knee replacement

352
00:09:21,850 --> 00:09:23,120
had less pain,

353
00:09:23,120 --> 00:09:23,830
less swelling

354
00:09:23,830 --> 00:09:25,410
and better early movement
than

355
00:09:25,410 --> 00:09:26,450
those who weren't.

356
00:09:27,050 --> 00:09:29,460
A 2025 review said the
same,

357
00:09:29,460 --> 00:09:30,560
and was clear the evidence

358
00:09:30,560 --> 00:09:31,630
is still limited.

359
00:09:31,670 --> 00:09:33,630
I probably sound like a
broken record

360
00:09:33,630 --> 00:09:35,100
to the people I work with.

361
00:09:35,400 --> 00:09:37,220
But after two years of
doing everything

362
00:09:37,220 --> 00:09:39,120
I was told and getting
nowhere,

363
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:40,210
you have no idea what it's

364
00:09:40,210 --> 00:09:41,860
like to sleep through the
night,

365
00:09:41,860 --> 00:09:43,260
say yes to the walk,

366
00:09:43,260 --> 00:09:44,520
and get my life back.

367
00:09:44,650 --> 00:09:45,880
So take it from me.

368
00:09:46,020 --> 00:09:47,470
Don't spend another year
waiting

369
00:09:47,470 --> 00:09:48,380
for it to settle.

370
00:09:49,020 --> 00:09:50,830
Don't spend two hundred a
session.

371
00:09:50,910 --> 00:09:52,270
More than ten thousand
people

372
00:09:52,270 --> 00:09:53,410
with pain after a knee

373
00:09:53,410 --> 00:09:55,690
replacement have already
tried this.

374
00:09:56,150 --> 00:09:57,870
Some had it worse than I
did.

375
00:09:57,990 --> 00:09:59,140
You can get the KenRelief

376
00:09:59,140 --> 00:10:01,110
wrap from their website,

377
00:10:01,110 --> 00:10:02,430
